{"artist": "Michael Jackson", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "j-pop": {"genre": "j-pop", "country_code": "jp", "country_name": "Japan", "summary": "J-pop (\u30b8\u30a7\u30a4\u30dd\u30c3\u30d7 \"jeipoppu\"), an abbreviation for Japanese pop, is a musical genre that entered the musical mainstream of Japan in the 1990s.  Modern J-pop has its roots in 1960s music, such as The Beatles, and replaced kay\u014dkyoku (\"Lyric Singing Music,\" a term for Japanese pop music from the 1920s to the 1980s) in the Japanese music scene.  The term was coined by the Japanese media to distinguish Japanese music from foreign music, and now refers to most Japanese popular music.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "back number", "streams": 1935388, "best_position": 4}, {"artist": "Mrs. GREEN APPLE", "streams": 1601565, "best_position": 2}, {"artist": "Kenshi Yonezu", "streams": 352794, "best_position": 21}, {"artist": "Vaundy", "streams": 140386, "best_position": 26}, {"artist": "King Gnu", "streams": 138931, "best_position": 72}, {"artist": "Mr.Children", "streams": 78269, "best_position": 61}, {"artist": "ASIAN KUNG-FU GENERATION", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ado", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Aimer", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "B'z", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BUMP OF CHICKEN", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Creepy Nuts", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "k-pop": {"genre": "k-pop", "country_code": "jp", "country_name": "Japan", "summary": "K-pop means Korean pop, which is\u00a0a musical genre, sometimes described more as an umbrella term, consisting of different music styles, including hip-hop, rap, jazz, r&b, dance, rock music and ballads. The name for the genre is first recorded in English around 1990\u201395. Strongly influenced by Western popular music, K-pop took off in 1992 with Seo Taiji and Boys, who incorporated rap, rock, and dance elements into Korean popular music.\nModern\u00a0K-pop \"idol\" culture\u00a0began later in the 1990s, as K-pop idol music grew into a\u00a0subculture.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": 175790, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Hearts2Hearts", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "KiiiKiii", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "LE SSERAFIM", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "NewJeans", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "TWICE", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "aespa", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "pop": {"genre": "pop", "country_code": "jp", "country_name": "Japan", "summary": "Pop music is a broad-term for many different types of music: The term is flexible, and the music labeled \"pop\" changes frequently. It usually refers to popular, appealing and mostly mainstream music with emphasis on catchy melodies and an accessible style, with songs that tend to have a short to medium length. Some subgenres may include synthpop, electropop, bubblegum, sophisti-pop, hyperpop and many others.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "ILLIT", "streams": 175790, "best_position": 8}, {"artist": "Vaundy", "streams": 140386, "best_position": 26}, {"artist": "Mr.Children", "streams": 78269, "best_position": 61}, {"artist": "AD\u00c9LA", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "ASIAN KUNG-FU GENERATION", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ado", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Aimer", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "B'z", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BTS", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "BUMP OF CHICKEN", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "post-punk": {"genre": "post-punk", "country_code": "jp", "country_name": "Japan", "summary": "Post-punk (originally called new musick) is a broad genre of music that emerged in late 1977 in the wake of punk rock. Post-punk musicians departed from punk's fundamental elements and raw simplicity, instead adopting a broader, more experimental approach that encompassed a variety of avant-garde sensibilities and non-rock influences. Inspired by punk's energy and do it yourself ethic but determined to break from rock cliches, artists experimented with styles like funk.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Arctic Monkeys", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "My Chemical Romance", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Cure", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Smiths", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "The Strokes", "streams": null, "best_position": null}]}, "r&b": {"genre": "r&b", "country_code": "jp", "country_name": "Japan", "summary": "R&B is a musical genre that began to develop as a distinct style in the early 1950s. Originally known as rhythm and blues, it was primarily created by African American musicians and drew influence from both blues and early rock 'n' roll, with significant interaction between these genres. Over time, musicians from different backgrounds adopted the style and introduced new elements. In the 1950s, artists like Muddy Waters contributed to shaping the genre by emphasizing faster melodies and energetic rhythms.", "url": null, "artists": [{"artist": "Ariana Grande", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Billie Eilish", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Britney Spears", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Bruno Mars", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Daft Punk", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Doja Cat", "streams": null, "best_position": null}, {"artist": "Drake", "streams": null, "be